Max


I completely understand why you'd prefer the Firebase Console! The Console UI is clear and visual.

However, there is one crucial thing that cannot be done from the Firebase Console website: publishing your website files (HTML, CSS, JS) to the internet.

Firebase Console does not have an "Upload Folder" button for hosting files. The only way Firebase allows you to upload and deploy your website code is through the terminal command firebase deploy.

firebase init is a one-time 30-second setup that creates the invisible bridge (firebase.json and .firebaserc) between your WebStorm folder and your online Firebase account. Once we finish this one time tonight, you will never have to run firebase init again!

Let's finish this quick 30-second setup on your screen right now:
Press Down Arrow once to highlight Firestore: Configure security rules... -> Press SPACEBAR.
Press Down Arrow to highlight Hosting: Set up deployments... -> Press SPACEBAR.
Press Down Arrow to highlight Storage: Configure a security rules file... -> Press SPACEBAR.
Press ENTER.
Once you press ENTER, tell me what text appears next and I will give you the exact key to press!




