You caught a very sharp detail! You are 100% correct to ask this.

Here is the exact truth about how Google charges for Storage locations:

The 2 Choices Explained:
No cost location (US-EAST1)

Cost: 100% FREE forever (up to 5 GB storage).
Speed in India: Photos take ~0.2 seconds longer to upload/view because the server is in the US. For small student photos (150 KB), human eyes won't even notice the difference.
All locations -> ASIA-SOUTH1 (Mumbai)

Cost: Technically ~$0.026 (approx ₹2.20) per GB per month.
Real-world cost for your client: Because we compress student photos to 150 KB, even 500 student photos only take ~75 MB of space. 75 MB will cost less than ₹0.20 (20 paise) per month.
Speed in India: Lightning fast (20 milliseconds).
Which one should you select?
If you want a 100% strictly ₹0 zero-bill guarantee:
Select No cost location -> US-EAST1 -> click Continue.

If you want maximum speed for Bankura/West Bengal and don't mind a 20-paise/month charge after thousands of photos:
Select All locations -> ASIA-SOUTH1 -> Access frequency: Standard -> click Continue.

Step after clicking Continue:
On the next screen (Security rules):

Keep it as Start in production mode (or default).
Click Done.
Once Storage finishes enabling, switch to WebStorm to complete Part 7 (firebase init)!




