The Project ID unique-infotech-cms is perfect.

Here is the complete step-by-step roadmap from your current screen all the way through to WebStorm setup. You can follow these parts one after another. If you get stuck at any step, stop and tell me!

PART 1: Finish Creating Project (Firebase Console)
On your screen right now, click the blue Continue button.
On the next screen ("Google Analytics"):
Turn the Google Analytics toggle switch OFF (Grey).
Click Create project.
Wait 10–15 seconds while Firebase initializes your project.
When you see "Your new project is ready", click Continue.
PART 2: Upgrade to Blaze Plan (Free Tier Safety)
In the top-left sidebar menu, look at the bottom-left corner where it says Spark plan (or click the Gear ⚙️ icon next to "Project Overview" -> Project settings).
Click Spark plan (or Modify plan).
Select Blaze (Pay as you go).
Select your Google Billing Account (or follow the prompt to link a billing profile if requested).
Click Purchase / Upgrade.
PART 3: Set Up $0.01 Budget Alert (Google Cloud Console)
Open a new tab in your browser and open:
https://console.cloud.google.com/billing
Ensure your project (unique-infotech-cms) or billing account is selected.
On the left menu, click Budgets & alerts.
Click + CREATE BUDGET at the top.
Name: Type Zero Cost Safety Alert. Click Next.
Amount Type: Select Specified amount.
Target amount: Type 0.01 (1 cent). Click Next.
Actions / Notifications: Ensure Email alerts to billing admins and users is checked.
Click Finish / Save.
PART 4: Enable Authentication Services
Switch back to your Firebase Console browser tab.
On the left sidebar menu, click Build -> Authentication.
Click Get started.
Under Native providers, click Email/Password:
Turn ON the first toggle (Enable). Leave "Email link" OFF.
Click Save.
Click Add new provider -> Select Google:
Turn ON Enable.
Under Project support email, select revertpixels@gmail.com.
Click Save.
PART 5: Enable Firestore Database (Mumbai Region)
On the left sidebar menu, click Build -> Firestore Database.
Click Create database.
Database location: Choose asia-south1 (Mumbai) from the dropdown menu. Click Next.
Security Rules: Select Start in production mode (Do NOT choose test mode).
Click Create / Enable. Wait until the empty database dashboard appears.
PART 6: Enable Cloud Storage (Mumbai Region)
On the left sidebar menu, click Build -> Storage.
Click Get started.
Security Rules: Select Start in production mode. Click Next.
Cloud Storage location: Ensure it shows asia-south1 (same as Firestore).
Click Done.
PART 7: Run Initializer in WebStorm Terminal
Switch to WebStorm.
Open the built-in Terminal at the bottom (or press Alt + F12).
Type firebase init and press ENTER.
Answer the questions on screen as follows:
Q1: Which Firebase features do you want to set up for this directory?

Move up/down with Arrow Keys.
Press SPACEBAR to mark * next to these 3 items:
Firestore: Configure security rules and indexes...
Hosting: Configure files for Firebase Hosting...
Storage: Configure a security rules file...
Press ENTER.
