I am a non-coder building a real production web app for a client. 
I only paste complete code files. Do not send partial code.

Project Name: Unique Infotech CMS (unique-infotech-cms)
Organisation: Bankura Zilla Youth Computer Training Centre / Unique Infotech

PLEASE READ THESE PROJECT DOCUMENTS IN YOUR LOCAL REPOSITORY FIRST:
1. docs/01-MASTER-PLAN.md      (Complete architecture & business logic)
2. docs/02-PROGRESS-LOG.md     (Latest built files & current state)
3. docs/03-DECISIONS.md        (Architectural & technical choices)
4. docs/04-DATABASE-MAP.md     (Firestore schema & relationships)
5. docs/05-FILE-INDEX.md        (Complete file & version registry)
6. docs/06-KNOWN-ISSUES.md     (Known bugs & tested constraints)

STRICT WORKING RULES:
1. Tech Stack: Plain Vanilla HTML + CSS + JavaScript ONLY. (NO React, NO Vue, NO Angular, NO npm/node_modules).
2. Send ONE full complete file at a time. Never send code snippets.
3. Wait for my "ok" or "done" before sending the next file.
4. Always update APP_VERSION in app.js and v= parameter in index.html when code changes.
5. NO Emojis anywhere in the UI. Use Lucide SVG icons only.
6. Design: Mobile-first responsive, custom dropdowns with icons, professional styling.
7. Hosting/Backend: Firebase Blaze Plan (must strictly respect free tier limits: browser image compression, targeted Firestore queries, pagination).
8. Data Isolation: Role-based security enforced via Firestore rules (Branch Heads see own branch data only).
9. Do not remove working features. Do not add unrequested external modules.
10. Treat this app with an ownership mentality: focus on high accuracy, security, auto-logout, "Collected By" audit tracking, and rock-solid UI execution.

