🚀 STEP 2: FIREBASE CONSOLE SETUP
Now let's configure your Firebase Console. Follow these clear steps on your browser:

1️⃣ Go to Firebase Console
Open Chrome/Brave and go to: https://console.firebase.google.com
Make sure you are logged in with your primary Google account.
2️⃣ Create Project
Click Add Project (or Create a Project).
Project Name: Type unique-infotech-cms (or bzyctc-cms).
Click Continue.
Google Analytics: You can turn this OFF (we don't need it for an internal tool) or leave it on.
Click Create Project and wait 10 seconds until it says "Your new project is ready".
Click Continue.
3️⃣ Upgrade to Blaze Plan (To enable Cloud Functions & Storage)
In the bottom-left corner of the Firebase Console, click on Spark (Free) or the gear icon ⚙️ → Usage and Billing.
Click Modify Plan → Select Blaze (Pay as you go).
Select your Google Cloud Billing Account (or add a card if requested).
Note: You will NOT be charged. We stay strictly inside the free monthly limits!
4️⃣ Set Budget Alert at $0.01 (Your Billing Safety Net)
Go to Google Cloud Console (https://console.cloud.google.com/billing).
Click on Budgets & Alerts on the left menu.
Click Create Budget.
Name: Zero Cost Safety Alert.
Target Amount: Set to $0.01 (or ₹1).
Email Alerts: Ensure your email checkbox is checked.
Click Save. Now if usage ever exceeds $0.00, Google will instantly email you!
5️⃣ Enable Firebase Authentication
Back in Firebase Console, click Build on the left menu → Authentication.
Click Get Started.
Under Sign-in method, enable TWO providers:
Email/Password: Click it → Enable Email/Password → Click Save.
Google: Click it → Enable Google → Set support email → Click Save.
6️⃣ Enable Firestore Database (Production Mode!)
Click Build → Firestore Database.
Click Create Database.
Location: Choose asia-south1 (Mumbai) (best speed for West Bengal, India!).
Security Rules: Choose Start in Production Mode (NOT Test Mode!).
Click Create / Enable.
7️⃣ Enable Firebase Storage
Click Build → Storage.
Click Get Started.
Choose Start in Production Mode.
Location: Keep default (asia-south1 or same as Firestore).
Click Done.
