Plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript will be used with no frameworks. A docs folder will hold the agreed markdown files. The structure will be mobile-first and highly scalable. No application code or logic files will be created yet.

The proposed folder structure is being drafted now. It includes a docs directory for master plans, progress logs, database maps, and handoff prompts. The public folder will hold the main HTML files and assets like images and CSS base styles.

The CSS directory will be split into base styles, components, layout, and pages. A main.css file will import all styles. The JavaScript folder will contain a Firebase config file and core modules for the app and authentication.

