I'm reviewing the project against their constraints to spot any remaining gaps. The core features already look solid, so I'll focus on high-value additions that fit their plain HTML/CSS/JS, Firebase free tier, and mobile-first requirements.

Offline PWA support would help Branch Heads work in areas with poor internet. Print-optimized receipts, ID cards, and certificates would improve usability. A global quick-search shortcut for students would speed up daily tasks.

Dashboard insights should surface actionable trends like overdue students or upcoming batch endings. A lightweight audit log would track who collected each payment. Bulk actions such as marking multiple students complete could speed up workflows. Course completion certificates and a full data export for Super Admins would add professional polish.

Dark mode is a quick CSS-variable addition. Empty states and loading skeletons would make the app feel premium. A session timeout would lock out idle users on shared computers.

A device and browser recommendation note would help users set up the app properly. Client-side WhatsApp sharing of receipts is free and avoids API dependencies. QR codes on receipts would enable future verification. An academic calendar for important dates would add useful planning tools.

