3. Youth Computer — Courses & Packages
Base Courses (Sem 1)

Created by Super Admin (name, duration, fees, installments, status…)
Fully dynamic
Packages

Super Admin creates packages:
Diploma (Sem 1 + Sem 2)
Advanced / 18-month (Sem 1 + Sem 2 + Sem 3)
While creating package, Super Admin selects which base courses belong to which semester.
A Sem 2 course cannot be taken unless Sem 1 of that package is completed.
Same rule for Sem 3.
Admission Form

Select Type → Certificate (Sem 1) / Diploma (Sem 2) / Advanced (Sem 3)
Select Course (filtered by type)
Upgrade / Continue Logic

Sem 1 → always fresh student
Sem 2 → system searches existing student
Found → auto-fill + carry forward history + tag “Completed Sem 1”
Not found (archived/deleted) → manual entry + past Sem 1 session details + still tagged “Completed Sem 1”
Sem 3 → searches Sem 2 records (which already carry Sem 1+2 tags)
Batches

Created only by Super Admin
Global (same batch available to all branches)
Name, course, timing, start/end date, status
