🧩 THE CONFUSION WE MUST SOLVE TOGETHER
The facts:

A 6-month course has 4 installments (example: ₹250 × 4)
A 12-month (2-sem) course has more installments
Client said: "Pay within 10th of the month, else ₹1/day fine"
But 4 installments ≠ 6 months of monthly payments
So the question is: When exactly is each installment DUE?

Here are the 3 most realistic ways computer centres in India usually handle this. Please read and tell me which one matches your client (or ask them):

📌 OPTION A — Fixed Installment Schedule per Batch
When Super Admin creates a Batch (e.g., Jan 2025 – June 2025), they also set 4 due dates:

text

Batch: Jan–June 2025 (CITA)
Installment 1 due: 10 Jan 2025
Installment 2 due: 10 Feb 2025
Installment 3 due: 10 Apr 2025
Installment 4 due: 10 May 2025
If student pays Installment 2 on 15 Feb → 5 days late → ₹5 fine
Very clear, very controllable
Super Admin sets the dates once per batch
📌 OPTION B — Equal Gap from Admission Date
Student joins → system auto-calculates 4 due dates based on course duration.

text

Admission: 5 Jan 2025
Installment 1: due 10 Jan (or immediately)
Installment 2: due ~10 Feb
Installment 3: due ~10 Apr
Installment 4: due ~10 May
Works even for late joiners
A bit more automatic
📌 OPTION C — Only “Pay by 10th” Rule, No Fixed Month Mapping
There are 4 installments with amounts
But there is no automatic due date
Branch Head manually decides “this installment is due this month”
Fine is calculated only when Branch Head marks it as overdue
Simplest to build, but easiest to make mistakes
📌 OPTION D — Something else the client does on paper
(Tell me how they currently write it in their register/Excel)

