Here is my confirmed understanding of Part 3.

✅ Confirmed Understanding — Part 3 (Courses & Admissions)
Course Packages (The Engine):
Super Admin creates Base Courses (Sem 1).
Super Admin creates "Packages" (Diploma = Sem 1 + Sem 2).
Super Admin creates (Advance = Sem 1 + Sem 2 + Sem 3).
Admission Form UI:
Dropdown 1: Select Type (1. Certificate/Sem 1 | 2. Diploma/Sem 2 | 3. Advanced/Sem 3).
Dropdown 2: Select Course (filters automatically based on Type).
The Upgrade Rules:
Type 1 (Sem 1): Always a fresh student admission.
Type 2 (Sem 2): Must search student first.
If found: Auto-fill data, carry forward.
If NOT found (archived): Allow manual form fill + ask for past Sem 1 details + auto-tag them as "Completed Sem 1".
Type 3 (Sem 3): Must search in Sem 2 records. Same auto-fill or manual-tag logic.
Batches: Global (same for all branches).
Compulsory Fields for Admission: Photo, Guardian details, Address, DOB, Gender, plus tracking for submitted documents (Aadhar/Birth Cert, Marksheet).
(Note on Free Storage: Since Firebase free storage is 5GB, I highly recommend we only require uploading the Student Photo to Firebase. For Aadhar/Marksheets, we will just use a checkbox saying "Physical Copy Submitted?" to save your cloud storage!)

📝 YOUR "TO-BE-DISCUSSED WITH CLIENT" LIST
As requested, I am keeping a safe list of things you need to ask the client later. I will remind you of these at the very end before we start!

