📖 My Complete Understanding of Your Project
I will now explain back to you everything I understand — in simple lines, as if I'm telling the story of this project. If I get anything wrong, you can correct me before we start.

🏢 PART 1: WHO THE CLIENT IS
The client is Bankura Zilla Youth Computer Training Centre, running since 2006.
It is a Government of West Bengal project under the Directorate of Youth Services.
Their head office is in Kenduadihi, Bankura.
They work in collaboration with "Unique Infotech".
They run computer training in two completely different ways under one single boss (Super Admin).
The brand name for their school program appears to be "Unique Compu Kids".
🏗️ PART 2: THE ORGANISATION STRUCTURE
At the very top sits ONE Super Admin who controls everything.
Under Super Admin there are TWO separate operations:
Youth Computer Centre (fixed-duration courses, like a college)
School Computer Program (monthly classes in schools, like a tuition)
The Youth Computer Centre has multiple branches (e.g., Bishnupur Sadar, Makurgram, Kenduadihi, and more can be added).
The School Computer Program has multiple schools where they go and teach.
Each branch has a Branch Head who runs that branch.
Each school will also have a School Head (same system as branches).
One person can be the head of multiple branches — so when they log in, they see a branch-selector to switch.
If a Branch Head's email is changed by Super Admin later, the old email loses access immediately.
Branch Heads and School Heads log in using Google Sign-in only (with their authorized email).
🎓 PART 3: THE COURSE SYSTEM (THE MOST IMPORTANT PART)
The organisation thinks in terms of 6-month base courses (CITA, CFAS, CDTP, CDTA, etc.).
A 12-month course = SEM 1 + SEM 2, where each SEM is a 6-month base course.
An 18-month course = SEM 1 + SEM 2 + SEM 3, where each SEM is a 6-month base course.
No student ever directly takes admission in a 12-month or 18-month course.
A student always starts from SEM 1 (a 6-month course).
When they finish SEM 1 and want to continue, the Branch Head takes a new admission for SEM 2 attached to the same student record.
If they want to continue further, another new admission for SEM 3 is taken.
The student's Student ID stays the same throughout — history is preserved.
All courses, fees, admission charges, installment counts are 100% DYNAMIC — Super Admin can create/edit them anytime from the admin panel without needing code changes.
When Super Admin creates a 12-month combined course, the system will let them pick which base courses are SEM 1 and SEM 2 from a dropdown.
💰 PART 4: THE FEE & PAYMENT SYSTEM
Every course has an Admission Fee + multiple Installments (number of installments is dynamic per course).
There is a Fine System:
Paid on or before 10th of the month = No fine
Paid after 10th = ₹1 per day late
The "Pay Fees" page is NOT a big list — it is a search box where admin types the Student ID, and only then the student's fee info loads (to save Firebase reads).
After typing Student ID, admin sees: course, batch, total fee, already paid, current due, next due date, previous payment history, and a "Record Payment" button.
When a payment is recorded, the system automatically updates the student's financial status AND creates a transaction record together (so nothing goes inconsistent).
The "Payment History" page is separate from Pay Fees — it is the complete ledger with filters (branch, date, student ID, course, batch, payment method, etc.).
No email receipts, no SMS, no WhatsApp — only printable PDF receipts generated from the system.
🏫 PART 5: THE SCHOOL COMPUTER PROGRAM
School Computer is NOT the same as Youth Computer — it uses a monthly fee model.
School students do NOT have courses, semesters, batches, or installments.
Each school student has: name, school, class, monthly fee amount, and monthly payment history.
Monthly fees, admission charges, structure — all dynamic (set by Super Admin per school or globally — to be decided later).
School Heads log in and manage only their own school's students, exactly like Branch Heads.
Super Admin sees all schools and all school payments.
🔐 PART 6: SECURITY & PERMISSIONS
A Branch Head can ONLY see:
Their own branch's students
Their own branch's admissions
Their own branch's payments
Their own branch's reports
A Branch Head CANNOT:
See other branches
Create courses or batches
Create other Branch Heads
Access Super Admin settings
Security must be enforced at the database level (Firestore Security Rules), not just by hiding menus.
Even if someone tries to hack the browser or change the URL manually, Firebase will reject their request.
Super Admin can see everything across both Youth and School sections.
📊 PART 7: THE DASHBOARD
The dashboard changes based on the Youth/School switcher at the top.
When Youth Computer is selected, dashboard shows: active branches, courses, batches, total students, admissions, fee collection, outstanding fees, recent payments, branch-wise summary.
When School Computer is selected, dashboard shows: active schools, students, monthly collection, outstanding monthly fees, recent payments, school-wise summary.
Dashboard is built smartly so it does not do heavy database reads just to show numbers (to stay in Firebase free limits).
📁 PART 8: THE ARCHIVE SYSTEM
Over years, old batches will pile up and eat Firebase storage.
Super Admin can archive old completed batches.
The archive workflow is:
Select old batch → Generate archive → Download ZIP → Verify → Then delete live data
The archive is a self-contained offline ZIP containing:
index.html + CSS + JS (viewer)
All students, payments, admissions data (as JSON)
All student photos (actual image files, not URLs)
Admin opens the ZIP, double-clicks index.html, and views the old batch without needing internet or Firebase.
The system will not delete live data until the archive is successfully downloaded and verified (safety confirmation).
📑 PART 9: REPORTS
Super Admin can download reports for: admissions, payments, dues, month-wise, branch-wise, course-wise — basically anything.
Branch Heads can download the same reports but only for their own branch.
Reports can be downloaded in Excel (CSV) and PDF formats.
👤 PART 10: STUDENT MANAGEMENT
Each student has: Student ID, name, photo (optional), DOB, gender, contact, address, guardian info, admission date, branch, current course/semester, current batch, course history, fee info, payment history, status.
Student ID format is still to be finalized (auto-generated like BIS-2025-0001 or manual — pending your decision).
Student photos will be compressed before upload (max 200KB) to save Firebase Storage (5GB free limit).
Previous payments, receipts, course history always stay connected to the same student record across upgrades.
🛠️ PART 11: TECHNOLOGY & SETUP
IDE: WebStorm on Windows (your PC).
Language: Plain HTML + CSS + Vanilla JavaScript (no React, Vue, Angular).
Hosting: Firebase Hosting.
Database: Firebase Firestore (production mode).
Authentication: Firebase Auth (Google Sign-in for Branch/School Heads, Email+Password for Super Admin).
File Storage: Firebase Storage (for student photos).
Secure operations: Firebase Cloud Functions where needed (e.g., archive generation, role management).
Billing plan: Firebase Blaze plan but strictly staying inside free tier limits by writing efficient code.
No public website — this is a private internal management tool, no domain name needed, we will use the free .web.app URL.
Ownership: You will create the Firebase project from your account and later transfer ownership to the client.
🎨 PART 12: DESIGN
The system is mobile-first and fully responsive (works on mobile, tablet, laptop, desktop).
Design is clean, professional, practical — not flashy, no unnecessary animations.
Colors will match the client's logo (you have the logo file ready).
Language: English only (no Bengali support needed).
Logo will be placed in the login page, top bar, and printable receipts.
📋 PART 13: WHAT WE WILL NOT BUILD
❌ No public institutional website
❌ No attendance system
❌ No student-facing portal
❌ No SMS / WhatsApp integration
❌ No email sending
❌ No complex accounting/HR/payroll/inventory/examination modules
❌ No unnecessary features — only what is actually needed
🚦 PART 14: HOW WE WILL BUILD IT
We will build in 6 phases, deploying and testing after each phase.
Phase 1: Login + empty dashboard shell + Youth/School switcher.
Phase 2: Super Admin core (branches, courses, batches, branch heads, org details).
Phase 3: Branch Head login + student registration + admissions + photo upload.
Phase 4: Pay fees + fine calculation + payment history + printable receipts.
Phase 5: Semester upgrades + School Computer module.
Phase 6: Reports + Archive system.
After each phase, you test it, confirm it works, then we move to the next.
📜 PART 15: HOW WE WORK TOGETHER
I send ONE full file at a time, you paste it in WebStorm.
For small changes, I give you exact Find & Replace instructions.
Every code change updates APP_VERSION in app.js and v= in index.html.
Before every deploy, you send me both version lines so I can verify they match.
After I confirm, you run firebase deploy in WebStorm terminal.
If something breaks, you paste the error, I fix it completely — not partially.
I will never assume you know something — I will explain everything simply.
I will not change working things without telling you why.
If you ask a question, no matter how small, it is important.
You are the project owner. I am your coding assistant. We build this together, step by step.
🚦 YOUR TURN
Please read these 100 points carefully.

✅ If everything is correct → say "All correct, let's start"
⚠️ If anything is wrong or missing → tell me the point number and what should be corrected
❓ If anything is unclear → ask me
I will not start writing code until you confirm this understanding is 100% correct. 🙏


