└── (any new 6-month course Super Admin creates)
A 12-month course = SEM 1 + SEM 2
Where SEM 1 and SEM 2 are each a 6-month base course.

text

Example: DITA (12 months)
├── SEM 1 = CITA (6 months)
└── SEM 2 = (another 6-month content)
An 18-month course = SEM 1 + SEM 2 + SEM 3
Where each SEM is a 6-month base course.

text

Example: 18-month course
├── SEM 1 = CITA (6 months)
├── SEM 2 = (6-month content)
└── SEM 3 = (6-month content)
Admission works like this:

text

Step 1: Student takes admission in SEM 1 (a 6-month course)
        → Pays SEM 1 fees
        → Studies for 6 months

Step 2: Student WANTS to continue? 
        → Branch Head takes NEW admission for SEM 2
        → Student's record stays SAME (not new student)
        → Previous history is preserved
        → Pays SEM 2 fees separately

Step 3: Student wants to continue more?
        → NEW admission for SEM 3
        → Same student record, history preserved
There is NO direct 12-month or 18-month admission.
A student always starts from SEM 1 (6 months) and upgrades step by step.

